From: Andrey Smirnov <andrey.smirnov@siderolabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "perf annotate: Fix build with NO_SLANG=1"

This reverts commit e97bd4417010c648acf9b1e509cfb77fc506e09e, which landed
in v6.18.52 as a backport of upstream 0e6c07a3c30c.

That commit adds a `u64 al_addr` parameter to the NO_SLANG stubs of
`hist_entry__tui_annotate()` / `__hist_entry__tui_annotate()`, because
upstream commit cd3466cd2639 ("perf c2c: Add annotation support to perf c2c
report") had already added the same parameter to the real implementations
and to every call site.

cd3466cd2639 was *not* backported to 6.18.y, so in v6.18.52 the stubs take
one argument more than the real declarations a few lines above them and one
more than the only call site:

  builtin-annotate.c:523:31: error: too few arguments to function
      'hist_entry__tui_annotate'; expected 4, have 3

perf-pkg builds without slang (no slang-devel in the toolchain), so it takes
the stub path and fails to build. The slang path is unaffected, which is why
this went unnoticed upstream.

`NO_ADDR` is introduced by the same commit and is unused anywhere else in
v6.18.52, so it is removed together with the stub signature change.

Temporary: drop this once 6.18.y either backports cd3466cd2639 or reverts
e97bd4417010, whichever comes first.

--- a/tools/perf/util/hist.h
+++ b/tools/perf/util/hist.h
@@ -708,8 +708,6 @@
 	bool			valid;
 	struct hist_entry	he;
 };
-
-#define NO_ADDR 0
 
 #ifdef HAVE_SLANG_SUPPORT
 #include "../ui/keysyms.h"
@@ -748,16 +746,14 @@
 static inline int __hist_entry__tui_annotate(struct hist_entry *he __maybe_unused,
 					     struct map_symbol *ms __maybe_unused,
 					     struct evsel *evsel __maybe_unused,
-					     struct hist_browser_timer *hbt __maybe_unused,
-					     u64 al_addr __maybe_unused)
+					     struct hist_browser_timer *hbt __maybe_unused)
 {
 	return 0;
 }
 
 static inline int hist_entry__tui_annotate(struct hist_entry *he __maybe_unused,
 					   struct evsel *evsel __maybe_unused,
-					   struct hist_browser_timer *hbt __maybe_unused,
-					   u64 al_addr __maybe_unused)
+					   struct hist_browser_timer *hbt __maybe_unused)
 {
 	return 0;
 }
